// =============================================================================
// Key Concepts Summary
// =============================================================================

/*
1. UnaryMiddleware vs StreamMiddleware:
   - UnaryMiddleware: For single request-response calls
   - StreamMiddleware: For streaming calls (wraps entire stream lifecycle)

2. StreamRecvMiddleware vs StreamSendMiddleware:
   - StreamRecvMiddleware: Intercepts each Recv() operation
   - StreamSendMiddleware: Intercepts each Send() operation

3. Option Batching:
   - WithUnaryOptions(): Group multiple unary options together
   - WithStreamOptions(): Group multiple streaming options together

4. Middleware Execution Order:
   - Options are applied right-to-left during client creation
   - Middleware executes left-to-right during runtime
   - Use endpoint.UnaryChain() to pre-compose middleware chains

5. Context-aware Middleware:
   - Use MiddlewareBuilder to access context values at construction time
   - Use WithUnaryMiddlewareBuilder() to register builders

6. Tail Functions:
   - tail_xxx options (like tail_ttstream) are automatically chained
   - Applied after all other options to ensure proper initialization order
*/

